No repositório do React, corrija a issue #28713: a regra react-hooks/rules-of-hooks (packages/eslint-plugin-react-hooks) não considera violação chamar um hook dentro de um loop do/while. Exemplo:

function ComponentWithHookInsideDoWhile() {
  do {
    useHookInsideLoop();
  } while (true);
}

O esperado é o mesmo erro que a regra já dá para hooks nos outros loops: React Hook "useHookInsideLoop" may be executed more than once. Possibly because it is called in a loop. React Hooks must be called in the exact same order in every component render. Acrescente testes em packages/eslint-plugin-react-hooks/__tests__/ESLintRulesOfHooks-test.js. Os testes do plugin rodam com: node ./scripts/jest/jest-cli.js packages/eslint-plugin-react-hooks
